00:50:31,578 --> 00:50:37,578
Hunger is a 2008 historical drama film about the 1981 Irish hunger strike.

11
00:55:34,736 --> 00:55:40,736
It was directed by Steve McQueen (in his feature directorial debut) and
starred Michael Fassbender, Liam Cunningham, and Liam McMahon.

12
01:00:37,894 --> 01:00:43,894
It premiered at the 2008 Cannes Film Festival, winning the
prestigious Caméra d'Or award for first-time filmmakers.

13
01:05:41,052 --> 01:05:47,052
It went on to win the Sydney Film Prize at the Sydney Film Festival, the Grand Prix of the Belgian Syndicate of Cinema Critics,
best picture from the Evening Standard British Film Awards, and received two BAFTA nominations, winning one.

14
01:10:44,210 --> 01:10:50,210
The film was also nominated for eight awards at the
2009 IFTAs, winning six at the event.

15
01:15:47,368 --> 01:15:53,368
The film stars Fassbender as Bobby Sands, the Provisional Irish Republican Army (IRA) member who led the second IRA hunger strike and participated in the no wash protest (led
by Brendan "The Dark" Hughes) in which Irish republican prisoners tried to regain political status after it had been revoked by the British government in 1976.

16
01:20:50,526 --> 01:20:56,526
It outlines events in the Maze Prison in the period leading
up to the hunger strike and its aftermath.

17
01:25:53,684 --> 01:25:59,684
The film explores themes of prison, police brutality,
prisoner, hunger strike, biography.

18
01:30:56,842 --> 01:31:02,842
The tone is dark and emotional.
